Z||000017||Formula88||12-11-2001||09:41 AM||||Ok, I remember your car from Williamsburg!  Loved the Koni decal on the fender.  Very tasteful and understated.  I was going off on how clean and pretty the car was, and your suspension.... I forgot about the turbo in the back !  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>How's she run?  Got any timeslips?  I'm weighing options for future engine swaps.  I like the 3.4 pushrod for it OEM Believability look, but it's not enough power.  A turbo could fix that, and still have the pretty "Fiero" engine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Although a 3.4DOHC Turbo would be pretty mean, too!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000018||Tigger||12-11-2001||10:33 AM||||Sweet Ride!!!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerwinter3.gif">           <BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR><A HREF="http://www.envy.nu/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>Tigger's Fiero Page</A>||||reg||14
Z||000019||turbo86se||12-11-2001||02:48 PM||||Thanks for all the compliements, I really appreciate it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'm done crying over the Colts blow-out last night, so I'll try to answer some questions.<P>fropuff, I looked for some other pics of the tips, and that's about the best I've got. <P>onfire, yep, it's a KONI sticker on my fender. I bought them at a Skip Barber race about five years ago in Savannah.<P>Jeff, that was a scary run, doing about 20-80 in a few seconds down that narrow street really got my heart pounding. I'm sure you noticed the holy-shI! look on my face when I got out! LOL <P>Formula88, which Fiero was yours? I've got pics of all of them. My SE runs perfect, shifts crisp, runs very smooth. I have no idea how much HP I'm running. Never been to the track. No hurry to get there either! Someday I will drop in a 3.4, but for now, with &lt;1000 miles per year, and it runs soooo good, I'm in no hurry. <P>Here's another pic at my parent's mountain house,<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86_at_Moose_tracks.jpg"> <P>||||reg||6
Z||000020||Formula88||12-11-2001||02:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by turbo86se:<BR><B>Formula88, which Fiero was yours? I've got pics of all of them.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, mine was a red Formula, in Stock Class, so it kinda blended in with the other Formulas.  Mine was 2nd to the last Formula in the row as you were coming into the parking lot.  I can pick mine out of the line, cuz I had my hood opened to the lower notch, and everyone else was full open.  I had to do <I>something</I> different.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I was amazed to see that yellow Formulas outnumbered the red ones.  That was weird.  And no black or silver ones at all.<P>I'm looking forward to the next show season.  Williamsburg was my first show.  I learned a lot.  Hope to see you at some shows next year!||||reg||14
